Cache: Context

Purpose:
  Define context caching policy, invalidation, and optimization.

CacheRules:
  [CC1]  Context MUST be cached to avoid re-analysis.
  [CC2]  Cache hit occurs when source unchanged (hash matches).
  [CC3]  Cache miss triggers re-build from scratch.
  [CC4]  Cache invalidation follows dependency graph.

CacheStructure:
  context-id:
    source: <list of sources>
    hash: <content hash>
    last-used: <timestamp>
    dependencies: <list of dependent contexts>

PullBasedLoading (Phase 151 — EXPAND protocol):
  InitialLoad:
    definition: every session/command auto-loads ONLY (a) the relevant
      INDEX.sdd routing table + (b) the command's InitialLoad manifest
      (2-3 files declared in its command spec).
    budget: initial load target < 1% of .sdd/ total content (previous
      behavior ~9% bulk load — now forbidden).
  EXPAND:
    definition: explicit request format for deeper content —
      `EXPAND <path-or-section>` — the AI asks, the section is provided.
    rule: only the requested section is returned; no adjacent pushes.
  PushBan:
    rule: heavy files (full skill trees, all phase specs, large analysis
      files) are NEVER proactively sent — wanted or unwanted, push is
      forbidden; everything beyond InitialLoad is EXPAND-only.
  Levels:
    LEVEL 0 (INDEX + manifest) — the ONLY auto-load tier.
    LEVEL 1-2 (details, references) — EXPAND-only (progressive disclosure
    is pull-based now).
  Caching:
    rule: InitialLoad manifests are cacheable — same manifest fingerprint
    => skip reload ([CC2] applies to manifest content too).

Optimization:
  Target: Relevant Context / Total Context > 80%
  Rule: Safety-critical tasks MUST NOT sacrifice relevance for efficiency.
  Evidence (external research 2026-09, RA-4): compiled/pulled context
    beats agent-discovered context by measured 5-6x token reduction
    (Moderne live demo 2026-04); structural retrieval lifted precision@5
    0.140 -> 0.478 vs grep baseline (Sourcegraph); auto-generated
    context files REDUCE agent success (arXiv 2602.11988) —
    human-authored routing + pull-based depth is the evidence-backed
    doctrine; full citations: .sdd/docs/analysis/external-research-2026-09.md

Navigation:
  CommandsIndex: @../commands/INDEX.sdd (InitialLoad declarations)
  ContextBuilder: @../runtime/context-builder.sdd
  PlanCache: @../../.claude/sdd/plan-cache.json

State: +
   (extended with PullBasedLoading / EXPAND protocol per Phase 151)
